module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Groupoids.QuasicoherentGrothendieck

/-!
# A separator for the quasi-coherent modules on a flat groupoid with a scheme of objects

Let `(U, R, s, t, c)` be a groupoid in algebraic spaces whose source and target are flat and whose
space of objects `U` is (the algebraic space of) a scheme of the site; the arrow space `R` is an
arbitrary algebraic space.  This is the shape of the groupoid of a presentation of an algebraic
stack by a scheme.  This file proves that `QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` has a separator, and hence, with
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Groupoids/QuasicoherentGrothendieck.lean`, that it is a
Grothendieck abelian category.

## The generator

The argument is that of Groupoids, Lemma 077U and of Groupoids in Spaces, Lemma 0780: every
quasi-coherent module `(ℱ, α)` on the groupoid is the union of submodules of bounded size, and
up to isomorphism there is only a set of modules of bounded size.

Choose a scheme `R'` and a surjective étale morphism `π : R' ⟶ R`, and put `s' = π ≫ s`,
`t' = π ≫ t`; these are morphisms of schemes `R' ⟶ U`, and they are flat.  The pullback
`α' = π^*α : t'^*ℱ ⟶ s'^*ℱ` is a morphism of quasi-coherent modules on the scheme `R'`, read on
the Zariski side through Descent, Proposition 03DX.  The closure step of the proof of Stacks 077U,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidCardinalGeneration.exists_transitionInvariant_mono_of_section`,
uses only such a morphism and the flatness of `s'`; it puts every local section of `ℱ` into a
quasi-coherent submodule `𝒵 ⊆ ℱ` generated by at most `κ` sections over each affine open, `κ`
bounding the affine opens of `U` and of `R'`, such that `α'` maps `t'^*𝒵` into `s'^*𝒵`.  Because
`π^*` is faithful and exact, `α` then maps `t^*𝒵` into `s^*𝒵`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_comp_eq_of_faithful`), and the restriction of `α` makes `𝒵` a
submodule of `(ℱ, α)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedQuasicoherentModule`).  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule`.

The `κ`-generated quasi-coherent modules on `U` have only a set of isomorphism classes
(Stacks 077M), and over a fixed underlying module the transition morphisms form a set; a set of
representatives is therefore a separating family,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_isSeparating_of_objects_eq`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule`: the closure step, for a module
  on a scheme `U` with a transition morphism along two morphisms `s`, `t` from an algebraic space,
  `s` flat.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_isSeparating_of_objects_eq`: a separating
  family of `u`-small index.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.hasSeparator_of_objects_eq` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.isGrothendieckAbelian_of_objects_eq`: the separator
  and the Grothendieck property.

## Implementation notes

The space of objects is asked to be *equal* to the algebraic space represented by a scheme `T`,
`G.objects = representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T`, rather than to be given as that space: the
space of objects of a groupoid is a field of the groupoid.  The comparison of Descent,
Proposition 03DX, is read across the equality
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence`), and the closure step is proved
for the represented space itself, where the comparison of inverse images along represented
morphisms with Zariski pullbacks,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representedAssociatedModulePullbackNatIso`, applies with no transport.

The atlas `R' ⟶ R` is written with source the anonymous algebraic space
`⟨yoneda.obj R', isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS R'⟩`, the source of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representedSpaceMap`, so that the categories of modules on `R'` reached
through the atlas and through the represented morphisms `R' ⟶ T` are syntactically the same.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0780](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0780)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 077M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/077M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

section Comparison

variable {C' C D : Type*} [Category* C'] [Category* C] [Category* D]

/-- A morphism `F_t M ⟶ F_s M`, read through comparisons `F_t ⋙ P ≅ G_t` and `F_s ⋙ P ≅ G_s` as a
morphism `G_t M ⟶ G_s M`. -/
def comparisonTransition {Ft Fs : C' ⥤ C} {P : C ⥤ D}
    {Gt Gs : C' ⥤ D} (it : Ft ⋙ P ≅ Gt) (is : Fs ⋙ P ≅ Gs) {M : C'}
    (α : Ft.obj M ⟶ Fs.obj M) : Gt.obj M ⟶ Gs.obj M :=
  it.inv.app M ≫ P.map α ≫ is.hom.app M

end Comparison

section Abstract

variable {C D : Type*} [Category* C] [Category* D] [Abelian C] [HasZeroMorphisms D]

/-- **A morphism factors through a monomorphism as soon as it does after a faithful left adjoint
functor.**  If `P f` factors through `P m`, then `f ≫ cokernel.π m` vanishes after `P`, which
preserves zero morphisms, hence vanishes, and `f` factors through the kernel of
`cokernel.π m`, which is `m`. -/
theorem exists_comp_eq_of_faithful (P : C ⥤ D) [P.Faithful] [P.IsLeftAdjoint] {X Y Z : C}
    (m : Y ⟶ Z) [Mono m] (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : P.obj X ⟶ P.obj Y) (h : g ≫ P.map m = P.map f) :
    ∃ k : X ⟶ Y, k ≫ m = f := by
  have h0 : f ≫ cokernel.π m = 0 := by
    apply P.map_injective
    rw [P.map_comp, ← h, Category.assoc, ← P.map_comp, cokernel.condition, P.map_zero,
      Limits.comp_zero, P.map_zero]
  exact ⟨Abelian.monoLift m f h0, Abelian.monoLift_comp m f h0⟩

/-- **A compatible transition morphism descends along a faithful left adjoint.**  Let
`F_t, F_s : C ⥤ D` and `P : D ⥤ D'`, with `P` faithful and a left adjoint, and let
`F_t ⋙ P ≅ G_t`, `F_s ⋙ P ≅ G_s`.  If `F_s ι` is a monomorphism and `β' : G_t E ⟶ G_s E` is
compatible along `ι` with `α : F_t M ⟶ F_s M` read through the two comparisons, then some
`β : F_t E ⟶ F_s E` is compatible with `α` along `ι`. -/
theorem exists_comp_eq_of_comparison {C' : Type*} [Category* C'] (Ft Fs : C' ⥤ C) (P : C ⥤ D)
    [P.Faithful] [P.IsLeftAdjoint] (Gt Gs : C' ⥤ D) (it : Ft ⋙ P ≅ Gt) (is : Fs ⋙ P ≅ Gs)
    {E M : C'} (ι : E ⟶ M) [Mono (Fs.map ι)] (α : Ft.obj M ⟶ Fs.obj M)
    (β' : Gt.obj E ⟶ Gs.obj E)
    (hβ' : β' ≫ Gs.map ι = Gt.map ι ≫ comparisonTransition it is α) :
    ∃ β : Ft.obj E ⟶ Fs.obj E, β ≫ Fs.map ι = Ft.map ι ≫ α := by
  refine exists_comp_eq_of_faithful P (Fs.map ι) (Ft.map ι ≫ α)
    (it.hom.app E ≫ β' ≫ is.inv.app E) ?_
  have ns := is.inv.naturality ι
  have nt := it.hom.naturality ι
  dsimp only [Functor.comp_map] at ns nt
  rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, ← ns, reassoc_of% hβ', comparisonTransition]
  simp only [Functor.comp_obj, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_app, Category.comp_id,
    Functor.map_comp]
  rw [← reassoc_of% nt, Iso.hom_inv_id_app_assoc]

end Abstract

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

section ArrowChart

variable (R : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)

/-- The chosen étale presentation of an algebraic space (Stacks 0263). -/
noncomputable abbrev arrowAtlasPresentation : Presentation B S hS R.obj R.property :=
  presentationOfIsAlgebraicSpace B S hS R.obj R.property

/-- The surjective étale atlas `R' ⟶ R` of an algebraic space by the scheme of its chosen
presentation. -/
noncomputable abbrev arrowAtlas :
    (⟨yoneda.obj (arrowAtlasPresentation R).U, isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _⟩ :
      AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ R :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (arrowAtlasPresentation R).toSpace

/-- The atlas of an algebraic space is étale. -/
theorem arrowAtlas_isEtale : IsEtale B S hS (arrowAtlas R).hom :=
  (isEtale_iff_presheaf_of_yoneda B S hS (arrowAtlasPresentation R).toSpace).2
    (arrowAtlasPresentation R).etale

/-- The inverse image of modules along the atlas of an algebraic space is faithful, the atlas
being surjective and étale. -/
theorem faithful_modulePullback_arrowAtlas : (modulePullback B S hS (arrowAtlas R)).Faithful :=
  faithful_modulePullback B S hS (arrowAtlasPresentation R).U (arrowAtlas R)
    (arrowAtlas_isEtale R) (arrowAtlasPresentation R).surjective

variable (T : BigFppfOver B S hS)

/-- The cardinal bounding the affine opens of a scheme `T` and of the scheme of the chosen atlas
of an algebraic space `R`. -/
noncomputable abbrev arrowAtlasCardinal : Cardinal.{u} :=
  max Cardinal.aleph0 (max (Cardinal.mk ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).affineOpens)
    (Cardinal.mk ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (arrowAtlasPresentation R).U).affineOpens))

variable {R T}

/-- The morphism of the site `R' ⟶ T` underlying the composite of the atlas `R' ⟶ R` of `R` with
a morphism `R ⟶ T` to a represented algebraic space. -/
noncomputable def arrowAtlasMap (f : R ⟶ representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) :
    (arrowAtlasPresentation R).U ⟶ T :=
  yoneda.preimage (arrowAtlas R ≫ f).hom

/-- The composite of the atlas with a morphism to a represented algebraic space is the
represented morphism `arrowAtlasMap f`. -/
theorem arrowAtlas_comp_eq (f : R ⟶ representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) :
    arrowAtlas R ≫ f = representedSpaceMap B S hS (arrowAtlasMap f) :=
  ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (yoneda.map_preimage (arrowAtlas R ≫ f).hom).symm

/-- The morphism of schemes underlying `arrowAtlasMap f` is flat when `f` is. -/
theorem flat_arrowAtlasMap (f : R ⟶ representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
    (hf : IsFlat B S hS f.hom) :
    Flat (B.inclusion.map (arrowAtlasMap f).left) := by
  have h1 : IsFlat B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS (arrowAtlasMap f)).hom := by
    rw [← arrowAtlas_comp_eq f]
    exact isFlat_comp B S hS (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _) R.property
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T) (arrowAtlas R).hom f.hom
      (isFlat_of_isEtale B S hS (arrowAtlas_isEtale R)) hf
  have h2 := (isFlat_iff_presheaf B S hS (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS _)
    (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T)
    (relativelyRepresentable_yoneda_map B S hS (arrowAtlasMap f))).1 h1
  exact (presheaf_yoneda_map_iff B S hS inferInstance (arrowAtlasMap f)).1 h2

end ArrowChart

section SchemeTransition

variable {T R' : BigFppfOver B S hS} (gt gs : R' ⟶ T)
  (M : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
    (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property)
  (α' : (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gt)).obj M.obj ⟶
    (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gs)).obj M.obj)

/-- The Zariski module on the scheme `T` corresponding to a quasi-coherent module on the
represented algebraic space of `T`. -/
noncomputable abbrev representedZariskiQcoh :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).ringCatSheaf).FullSubcategory :=
  (representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.obj M

/-- The identification of the associated module of `representedZariskiQcoh M` with `M`. -/
noncomputable def representedZariskiQcohIso :
    (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T).obj (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj ≅ M.obj :=
  (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, u}
    (representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS T)).ι.mapIso
      ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).counitIso.app M)

/-- A morphism `g_t^*M ⟶ g_s^*M` along two morphisms of represented algebraic spaces, read as a
morphism between the associated modules of the Zariski pullbacks. -/
noncomputable abbrev associatedRepresentedTransition :
    (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS R').obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (B.inclusion.map gt.left)).obj
          (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj) ⟶
      (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS R').obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (B.inclusion.map gs.left)).obj
          (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj) :=
  comparisonTransport
    (representedAssociatedModulePullbackNatIso B S hS gt
      (relativelyRepresentable_yoneda_map B S hS gt))
    (representedAssociatedModulePullbackNatIso B S hS gs
      (relativelyRepresentable_yoneda_map B S hS gs))
    (representedZariskiQcohIso M) α'

/-- **A transition morphism along represented morphisms, on the Zariski side.**  The unique
morphism `g_t^*𝓕 ⟶ g_s^*𝓕` of Zariski modules on `R'` whose associated module is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.associatedRepresentedTransition`, for `𝓕` the Zariski module
corresponding to `M`; it exists because `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` is fully faithful on quasi-coherent
modules. -/
noncomputable def representedZariskiTransition :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (B.inclusion.map gt.left)).obj (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback (B.inclusion.map gs.left)).obj (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj :=
  ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS R').fullyFaithfulFunctor.preimage
    (ObjectProperty.homMk (associatedRepresentedTransition gt gs M α') :
      (representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS R').functor.obj
          (qcohSchemePullback gt (representedZariskiQcoh M)) ⟶
        (representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS R').functor.obj
          (qcohSchemePullback gs (representedZariskiQcoh M)))).hom

/-- The associated module of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representedZariskiTransition` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.associatedRepresentedTransition`. -/
theorem map_representedZariskiTransition :
    (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS R').map (representedZariskiTransition gt gs M α') =
      associatedRepresentedTransition gt gs M α' :=
  congrArg (fun k => k.hom)
    ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS R').fullyFaithfulFunctor.map_preimage
      (ObjectProperty.homMk (associatedRepresentedTransition gt gs M α') :
        (representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS R').functor.obj
            (qcohSchemePullback gt (representedZariskiQcoh M)) ⟶
          (representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS R').functor.obj
            (qcohSchemePullback gs (representedZariskiQcoh M))))

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry in
/-- **Every local section of a module with a transition morphism along represented morphisms lies
in a bounded invariant submodule.**  Let `g_t, g_s : R' ⟶ T` be morphisms of the site with `g_s`
flat, `M` a quasi-coherent module on the represented algebraic space of `T` and
`α' : g_t^*M ⟶ g_s^*M`.  For every local section `x` of the Zariski module corresponding to `M`
there are a quasi-coherent `κ`-generated Zariski module `𝒵` on `T`, `κ` bounding the affine opens
of `T` and of `R'`, a monomorphism `ι` from its associated module `E` to `M` and a morphism
`β' : g_t^*E ⟶ g_s^*E` compatible with `α'` along `ι`, such that any two morphisms out of `M`
which agree after `ι` agree on `x`.

This is the closure step of Stacks 077U,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupoidCardinalGeneration.exists_transitionInvariant_mono_of_section`,
run on the Zariski side and carried back along the comparison of Stacks 03DX (2). -/
theorem exists_bounded_represented_invariant_submodule [Flat (B.inclusion.map gs.left)]
    {κ : Cardinal.{u}} (hκ : Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ κ)
    (hU : Cardinal.mk ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).affineOpens ≤ κ)
    (hR : Cardinal.mk ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj R').affineOpens ≤ κ)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Opens)
    (x : Γ(((representedZariskiQcoh M).obj : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules), O)) :
    ∃ (Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules) (_ : Z.IsQuasicoherent)
      (E : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
        (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property)
      (ι : E.obj ⟶ M.obj)
      (β' : (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gt)).obj E.obj ⟶
        (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gs)).obj E.obj),
      CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z κ ∧
      Nonempty (E.obj ≅ (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T).obj Z) ∧
      Mono ι ∧
      β' ≫ (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gs)).map ι =
        (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gt)).map ι ≫ α' ∧
      ∀ (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
          (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property) (a b : M ⟶ N),
        ι ≫ a.hom = ι ≫ b.hom →
          Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.map a).hom O x =
            Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.map b).hom O x := by
  classical
  let eU := representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T
  have : (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj.IsQuasicoherent := (representedZariskiQcoh M).property
  have hclos := GroupoidCardinalGeneration.exists_transitionInvariant_mono_of_section
      (U := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
      (R := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj R')
      (B.inclusion.map gt.left) (B.inclusion.map gs.left)
      (representedZariskiQcoh M).obj (representedZariskiTransition gt gs M α') hκ hU hR O x
  obtain ⟨Z, ιZ, βZ, hιZ, hZ, hZκ, hβZ, ⟨y, hy⟩⟩ := hclos
  let Zq : (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).ringCatSheaf).FullSubcategory := ⟨Z, hZ⟩
  let ιq : Zq ⟶ representedZariskiQcoh M := ObjectProperty.homMk ιZ
  have hβ' := comparisonTransportBack_comm
    (representedAssociatedModulePullbackNatIso B S hS gt
      (relativelyRepresentable_yoneda_map B S hS gt))
    (representedAssociatedModulePullbackNatIso B S hS gs
      (relativelyRepresentable_yoneda_map B S hS gs))
    (representedZariskiQcohIso M) α' _ (map_representedZariskiTransition gt gs M α') ιZ βZ hβZ
  let : (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, u}
      (representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS T)).IsClosedUnderKernels :=
    isClosedUnderKernels_quasicoherentSheaves_schemeUniverse B S hS (yoneda.obj T)
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T)
  let : (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, u}
      (representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS T)).IsClosedUnderCokernels :=
    isClosedUnderCokernels_quasicoherentSheaves B S hS (yoneda.obj T)
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T)
  have hpc : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1,
      u, u, u} (representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS T)).ι :=
    (@SheafOfModules.preservesFiniteLimits_ι_isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, u} _ _ _
      (representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS T) _ _ _ _ _).preservesFiniteLimits WalkingCospan
  have hιq : Mono ιq := (ObjectProperty.ι _).mono_of_mono_map hιZ
  have i1 : eU.functor.PreservesMonomorphisms :=
    Functor.preservesMonomorphisms_of_adjunction eU.symm.toAdjunction
  have i2 : (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite.{u + 1, u, u, u}
      (representedStructureRingSheaf B S hS T)).ι.PreservesMonomorphisms :=
    @preservesMonomorphisms_of_preservesLimitsOfShape _ _ _ _ _ hpc
  have hLι : Mono ((representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T).map ιZ) :=
    @Functor.map_mono _ _ _ _ _ i2 _ _ (eU.functor.map ιq)
      (@Functor.map_mono _ _ _ _ eU.functor i1 _ _ ιq hιq)
  have hε : Mono (representedZariskiQcohIso M).hom :=
    ⟨fun g h hgh => by
      simpa only [Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id] using
        congrArg (· ≫ (representedZariskiQcohIso M).inv) hgh⟩
  refine ⟨Z, hZ, ⟨(representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T).obj Z,
      (eU.functor.obj Zq).property⟩, _, _, hZκ, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩,
    mono_comp' hLι hε, hβ', ?_⟩
  intro N a b hab
  have key : eU.functor.map ιq ≫ eU.counit.app M ≫ a =
      eU.functor.map ιq ≫ eU.counit.app M ≫ b := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    simp only [representedZariskiQcohIso, Functor.mapIso_hom] at hab
    exact hab
  have h2 : ιq ≫ eU.inverse.map a = ιq ≫ eU.inverse.map b :=
    comp_inverse_map_eq_of_counit eU ιq _ _ key
  have h3 := congrArg (fun k => Scheme.Modules.Hom.app
    (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T) k.hom O y) h2
  rw [← hy]
  simp only [ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory.comp_hom] at h3
  exact h3

end SchemeTransition

section Core

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

variable {T R' : BigFppfOver B S hS} {R : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
  (π : (⟨yoneda.obj R', isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS R'⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) ⟶ R)

/-- The inverse image along `π ≫ f` compared with the inverse image along a represented morphism
`g` equal to it. -/
noncomputable def atlasPullbackIso (f : R ⟶ representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) (g : R' ⟶ T)
    (h : π ≫ f = representedSpaceMap B S hS g) :
    modulePullback B S hS f ⋙ modulePullback B S hS π ≅
      modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS g) :=
  modulePullbackCompIso B S hS π f ≪≫ eqToIso (congrArg (modulePullback B S hS) h)

variable (s t : R ⟶ representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) (gs gt : R' ⟶ T)
  (hgs : π ≫ s = representedSpaceMap B S hS gs) (hgt : π ≫ t = representedSpaceMap B S hS gt)
  (M : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
    (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property)
  (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj M.obj ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj M.obj)

/-- **A transition morphism compatible on the atlas is compatible on `R`.**  If `β'` is
compatible along `ι` with
`comparisonTransition (atlasPullbackIso π t gt hgt) (atlasPullbackIso π s gs hgs) α`, and `s^*ι` is
a monomorphism, then `t^*ι ≫ α` factors through `s^*ι`. -/
theorem exists_comp_eq_of_atlasTransition [(modulePullback B S hS π).Faithful]
    {E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
      (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property} (ι : E ⟶ M.obj)
    [Mono ((modulePullback B S hS s).map ι)]
    (β' : (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gt)).obj E ⟶
      (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gs)).obj E)
    (hβ' : β' ≫ (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gs)).map ι =
      (modulePullback B S hS (representedSpaceMap B S hS gt)).map ι ≫
        comparisonTransition (atlasPullbackIso π t gt hgt) (atlasPullbackIso π s gs hgs) α) :
    ∃ β : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj E ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj E,
      β ≫ (modulePullback B S hS s).map ι = (modulePullback B S hS t).map ι ≫ α :=
  have := modulePullback_isLeftAdjoint π
  exists_comp_eq_of_comparison (modulePullback B S hS t) (modulePullback B S hS s)
    (modulePullback B S hS π) _ _ (atlasPullbackIso π t gt hgt) (atlasPullbackIso π s gs hgs)
    ι α β' hβ'

include gt hgs hgt in
/-- **Every local section of a module with a transition morphism lies in a bounded invariant
submodule.**  Let `T` be a scheme, `R` an algebraic space, `s, t : R ⟶ T` with `s` flat, `M` a
quasi-coherent module on `T` and `α : t^*M ⟶ s^*M`.  For every local section `x` of the Zariski
module corresponding to `M` there are a quasi-coherent `κ`-generated Zariski module `𝒵` on `T`,
`κ = arrowAtlasCardinal R T`, a monomorphism `ι` from its associated module `E` to `M` and a
morphism `β : t^*E ⟶ s^*E` compatible with `α` along `ι`, such that any two morphisms out of `M`
which agree after `ι` agree on `x`.

The closure step of Stacks 077U is run on the atlas scheme `R'` of `R`, where `α` becomes a
morphism of Zariski modules; the resulting `β` on `R'` descends to `R` because the inverse image
along the atlas is faithful and `s^*ι` is a monomorphism. -/
theorem exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_atlas [(modulePullback B S hS π).Faithful]
    [Flat (B.inclusion.map gs.left)] (hs : IsFlat B S hS s.hom) {κ : Cardinal.{u}}
    (hκ : Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ κ)
    (hU : Cardinal.mk ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).affineOpens ≤ κ)
    (hR : Cardinal.mk ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj R').affineOpens ≤ κ)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Opens)
    (x : Γ(((representedZariskiQcoh M).obj : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules), O)) :
    ∃ (Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules) (_ : Z.IsQuasicoherent)
      (E : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
        (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property)
      (ι : E.obj ⟶ M.obj)
      (β : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj E.obj ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj E.obj),
      CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z κ ∧
      Nonempty (E.obj ≅ (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T).obj Z) ∧
      Mono ι ∧
      β ≫ (modulePullback B S hS s).map ι = (modulePullback B S hS t).map ι ≫ α ∧
      ∀ (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
          (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property) (a b : M ⟶ N),
        ι ≫ a.hom = ι ≫ b.hom →
          Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.map a).hom O x =
            Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.map b).hom O x := by
  have h1 := exists_bounded_represented_invariant_submodule gt gs M
      (comparisonTransition (atlasPullbackIso π t gt hgt) (atlasPullbackIso π s gs hgs) α)
      hκ hU hR O x
  obtain ⟨Z, hZ, E, ι, β', hZκ, hE, hι, hβ', hdet⟩ := h1
  have := hι
  have := modulePullback_isLeftAdjoint π
  have : Mono ((modulePullback B S hS s).map ι) := mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat s hs ι hι
  have h2 := exists_comp_eq_of_atlasTransition π s t gs gt hgs hgt M α ι β' hβ'
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := h2
  exact ⟨Z, hZ, E, ι, β, hZκ, hE, hι, hβ, hdet⟩

/-- **Every local section of a module with a transition morphism lies in a bounded invariant
submodule**, for the cardinal `arrowAtlasCardinal R T` attached to the chosen atlas of `R`.  This
is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_atlas` at that atlas. -/
theorem exists_bounded_invariant_submodule {R : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (s t : R ⟶ representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T) (hs : IsFlat B S hS s.hom)
    (M : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
      (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj M.obj ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj M.obj)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Opens)
    (x : Γ(((representedZariskiQcoh M).obj : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules), O)) :
    ∃ (Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules) (_ : Z.IsQuasicoherent)
      (E : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
        (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property)
      (ι : E.obj ⟶ M.obj)
      (β : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj E.obj ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj E.obj),
      CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z (arrowAtlasCardinal R T) ∧
      Nonempty (E.obj ≅ (representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T).obj Z) ∧
      Mono ι ∧
      β ≫ (modulePullback B S hS s).map ι = (modulePullback B S hS t).map ι ≫ α ∧
      ∀ (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).obj
          (representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T).property) (a b : M ⟶ N),
        ι ≫ a.hom = ι ≫ b.hom →
          Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.map a).hom O x =
            Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T).inverse.map b).hom O x := by
  have := faithful_modulePullback_arrowAtlas R
  have := flat_arrowAtlasMap s hs
  exact exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_atlas (arrowAtlas R) s t (arrowAtlasMap s)
    (arrowAtlasMap t) (arrowAtlas_comp_eq s) (arrowAtlas_comp_eq t) M α hs (le_max_left _ _)
    ((le_max_left _ _).trans (le_max_right _ _)) ((le_max_right _ _).trans (le_max_right _ _)) O x

end Core

section ObjectsEq

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

variable {T : BigFppfOver B S hS} {U : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
  (hU : U = representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)

/-- The equivalence of Descent, Proposition 03DX, between quasi-coherent Zariski modules on a
scheme `T` and quasi-coherent modules on an algebraic space `U` equal to the algebraic space of
`T`. -/
noncomputable def objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence :
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).ringCatSheaf).FullSubcategory ≌
      QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS U.obj U.property :=
  hU ▸ representedQuasicoherentSchemeEquivalence B S hS T

/-- The associated module functor from Zariski modules on a scheme `T` to the modules on an
algebraic space `U` equal to the algebraic space of `T`. -/
noncomputable def objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor :
    ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules ⥤ Modules.{u, u} B S hS U.obj U.property :=
  hU ▸ representedAssociatedModuleFunctor B S hS T

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule` for an algebraic space `U` equal
to the algebraic space of a scheme `T`, read through that equality. -/
theorem exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_eq {R : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (s t : R ⟶ U)
    (hs : IsFlat B S hS s.hom)
    (M : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS U.obj U.property)
    (α : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj M.obj ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj M.obj)
    (O : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Opens)
    (x : Γ((((objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence hU).inverse.obj M).obj :
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules), O)) :
    ∃ (Z : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules) (_ : Z.IsQuasicoherent)
      (E : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS U.obj U.property)
      (ι : E.obj ⟶ M.obj)
      (β : (modulePullback B S hS t).obj E.obj ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS s).obj E.obj),
      CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated Z (arrowAtlasCardinal R T) ∧
      Nonempty (E.obj ≅ (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor hU).obj Z) ∧
      Mono ι ∧
      β ≫ (modulePullback B S hS s).map ι = (modulePullback B S hS t).map ι ≫ α ∧
      ∀ (N : QuasicoherentSheaves.{u, u} B S hS U.obj U.property) (a b : M ⟶ N),
        ι ≫ a.hom = ι ≫ b.hom →
          Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence hU).inverse.map a).hom O x =
            Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (X := (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
              ((objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence hU).inverse.map b).hom O x := by
  subst hU
  exact exists_bounded_invariant_submodule s t hs M α O x

end ObjectsEq

namespace QuasicoherentModule

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry

variable {A : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- **A separating family of quasi-coherent modules on a flat groupoid whose space of objects is
a scheme.**  Let `(U, R, s, t, c)` be a groupoid in algebraic spaces with `s` flat and `U` the
algebraic space of a scheme `T`.  There is a family of quasi-coherent modules on the groupoid,
indexed by a type in the universe of the schemes, which is separating in `QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)`.

Every local section of a quasi-coherent module `(ℱ, α)` on the groupoid lies in a submodule
`(𝒵^a, β)` with `𝒵` a `κ`-generated quasi-coherent Zariski module on `T`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_bounded_invariant_submodule`, the restriction being a module on
the groupoid by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictedQuasicoherentModule`); the `κ`-generated
quasi-coherent modules have only a set of isomorphism classes (Stacks 077M) and over a fixed
underlying module the transition morphisms form a set, so a set of representatives
separates. -/
theorem exists_isSeparating_of_objects_eq (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A)
    {T : BigFppfOver B S hS} (hU : G.objects = representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
    (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom) :
    ∃ (β : Type u) (f : β → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G),
      (ObjectProperty.ofObj f).IsSeparating := by
  classical
  let κ := arrowAtlasCardinal G.arrows T
  let eU := objectsQuasicoherentEquivalence hU
  let Pz : ObjectProperty ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules := fun M =>
    M.IsQuasicoherent ∧ CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated M κ
  have : ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{u}
      (fun M : ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).Modules =>
        CardinalGeneration.IsCardinalGenerated M κ) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.CardinalGenerated.essentiallySmall_isCardinalGenerated
      (X := ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T).toRingedSpace) κ
  have : ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.{u} Pz :=
    ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.of_le fun _ h => h.2
  obtain ⟨Q, hQsmall, -, hPQ⟩ := ObjectProperty.EssentiallySmall.exists_small_le.{u} Pz
  have := hQsmall
  let W : Subtype Q → Modules.{u, u} B S hS G.objects.obj G.objects.property :=
    fun z => (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor hU).obj z.1
  have : LocallySmall.{u} (Modules.{u, u} B S hS G.arrows.obj G.arrows.property) :=
    locallySmall_modules_smallEtale B S hS _ _
  let Aset : Subtype Q → Type (u + 1) := fun z =>
    {a : (modulePullback B S hS G.target).obj (W z) ⟶ (modulePullback B S hS G.source).obj (W z) //
      ∃ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (e : Y.F.obj ≅ W z), transportedTransition Y e = a}
  let Ind := Σ z : Subtype Q, Aset z
  have : Small.{u} Ind := inferInstance
  let rep : Ind → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G := fun i => Classical.choose i.2.2
  have hrep : ∀ (Y : QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) (z : Subtype Q) (e : Y.F.obj ≅ W z),
      ∃ i : Ind, Nonempty (rep i ≅ Y) := by
    intro Y z e
    let i : Ind := ⟨z, ⟨transportedTransition Y e, Y, e, rfl⟩⟩
    obtain ⟨e₀, h₀⟩ := Classical.choose_spec i.2.2
    exact ⟨i, ⟨isoOfTransportedTransitionEq e₀ e h₀⟩⟩
  let fG : Shrink.{u} Ind → QuasicoherentModule B S hS G :=
    fun b => rep ((equivShrink Ind).symm b)
  refine ⟨Shrink.{u} Ind, fG, ?_⟩
  intro M M' a b hab
  apply QuasicoherentModule.Hom.ext
  have hq : eU.inverse.map (ObjectProperty.homMk a.hom : M.F ⟶ M'.F) =
      eU.inverse.map (ObjectProperty.homMk b.hom : M.F ⟶ M'.F) := by
    apply ObjectProperty.hom_ext
    refine scheme_modules_hom_ext_of_app_apply _ _ fun O x => ?_
    have h0 := exists_bounded_invariant_submodule_of_eq hU G.source G.target hs M.F M.alpha O x
    obtain ⟨Z, hZ, E, ι, β, hZκ, ⟨eE⟩, hι, hβ, hdet⟩ := h0
    have hm := fun {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : X ⟶ G.objects) (hf : IsFlat B S hS f.hom) =>
      mono_modulePullback_map_of_isFlat f hf ι hι
    have hc := hm _ (isFlat_comp_comp_source G hs)
    have he := hm _ (isFlat_identityArrow_comp_source G)
    obtain ⟨Z₀, hZ₀, ⟨eZ⟩⟩ := hPQ Z ⟨hZ, hZκ⟩
    have e1 : E.obj ≅ W ⟨Z₀, hZ₀⟩ := eE ≪≫ (objectsAssociatedModuleFunctor hU).mapIso eZ
    have hi := hrep (restrictedQuasicoherentModule M E ι β hβ hc he) ⟨Z₀, hZ₀⟩ e1
    obtain ⟨i, ⟨ei⟩⟩ := hi
    have hmem : ObjectProperty.ofObj fG (rep i) :=
      (ObjectProperty.ofObj_iff fG _).2 ⟨equivShrink Ind i, by simp [fG]⟩
    have h := hab (rep i) hmem (ei.hom ≫ restrictedQuasicoherentModuleHom M E ι β hβ hc he)
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, cancel_epi] at h
    exact hdet M'.F (ObjectProperty.homMk a.hom) (ObjectProperty.homMk b.hom)
      (congrArg QuasicoherentModule.Hom.hom h)
  exact congrArg (fun k => k.hom) (eU.inverse.map_injective hq)

/-- **`QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` has a separator**, for a groupoid with flat source whose space of
objects is the algebraic space of a scheme: a coproduct of the separating family of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuasicoherentModule.exists_isSeparating_of_objects_eq`. -/
theorem hasSeparator_of_objects_eq (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A)
    {T : BigFppfOver B S hS} (hU : G.objects = representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
    (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom) : HasSeparator (QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) := by
  obtain ⟨β, f, hf⟩ := exists_isSeparating_of_objects_eq G hU hs
  exact ⟨∐ f, (isSeparator_sigma f).2 hf⟩

/-- **The quasi-coherent modules on a flat groupoid whose space of objects is a scheme form a
Grothendieck abelian category.** -/
theorem isGrothendieckAbelian_of_objects_eq (G : GroupoidInAlgebraicSpaces B S hS A)
    {T : BigFppfOver B S hS} (hU : G.objects = representedAlgebraicSpace B S hS T)
    (hs : IsFlat B S hS G.source.hom) (ht : IsFlat B S hS G.target.hom) :
    letI := abelian_of_closure G hs ht
    IsGrothendieckAbelian.{u} (QuasicoherentModule B S hS G) :=
  let := abelian_of_closure G hs ht
  have := hasSeparator_of_objects_eq G hU hs
  isGrothendieckAbelian_of_hasSeparator G hs ht

end QuasicoherentModule

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

